What this scene shows about Vlaems

Register stratification: The colloquial scenes used da's, der, nie zot; this one uses so, zij, ziele, geleiden — a formal, liturgical layer.

Latin liturgy: The Church preserves Latin fragments (Benedicte, Domine; Requiem aeternam; In nomine Patris), just as in real Flemish history.

Archaic morphology: Final -e on nouns (ziele) and subjunctive zij appear only in ritual language.

Poetic parallelism: De zee geeft, en de zee neemt — biblical-style parallelism, common in coastal ritual.

French loans in ritual: kameraad, oratie (if used), kapelle — Romance vocabulary dominates both commerce and liturgy.

Separable verbs in formal register: teruggenomen still splits: heeft ... teruggenomen.

The great return: de grote weerkeer — a uniquely Vlaems eschatological concept, blending Christian resurrection with the sea's cyclical tides.

